  [-]load <xe file>: Loads the given xmos executable file
  [-]path <from ref> <to ref>: Sets a path start and end points
  [-]function <name>: Sets a path to trace a given function
  [-]list <type>: Lists all of the given <type> in the currently loaded executable
  [-]status: Display current status
  [-]summary <path id | level>: Display timing summary for paths/functions
  [-]asm <path id>: Display annotated assembly for given path id
  [-]src <path id> <source file>: Display annotated source file for given path id
  [-]mix <path id> <source file>: Display annotated source file + assembly instructions for the given path id
  [-]trace <path id | level>: Display instruction trace for the given path id
  [-]loop <path> <scope> <iterations>: Sets the number of iterations for the given path
  [-]time <pc> <mode> <value>: Sets the time taken for the instruction at the given pc
  [-]source <file name>: Sources the given command file
  [-]history: Displays the command history
  [-]pwd: Displays the current working directory
  [-]config <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Configures the given option
  [-]help [command]: Displays help message for the given command
  [-]exit: Quits the shell
  [-]timebound <int (ns)> : returns PASS of FAIL if the worst case is less than the time bound
  [-]cyclebound <int (cycles)> : returns PASS of FAIL if the worst case is less than the cycle bound
  [-]label <CodeRef> <label>: adds a label to the given pc
  [-]excluded <add/remove> <ref>: Adds or removes the given reference to the excluded list (post analysis action)
  [-]prohibited <add/remove> <ref>: Adds or removes the given reference to the prohibited list (during analysis action)
  [-]required <add/remove> <ref>: Adds or removes the given reference to the required list (post analysis action)
